.TH KOBRA-LAN 1 "2026-11-02" "Kobra LAN CLI" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kobra-lan \- experimental direct Anycubic Kobra X LAN client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kobra-lan
.RI [ global-options ] " command " [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Inspect G-code locally and perform explicitly reviewed LAN operations with JSON
output. Upload and print start require separate reviewed execution flags.
Use the help for each command before attempting an operation.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
Show commands and options. Each command also accepts --help.
.TP
.B --version
Show the application version.
.TP
.BI --config " path"
Select private configuration (default ~/.config/kobra-lan/config.json).
.TP
.BI --state-dir " path"
Select durable state (default ~/.local/share/kobra-lan/uploads).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 indicates success; 2 indicates protocol/validation failure; 3 indicates
configuration/network failure. Operations are never retried automatically.
.SH FILES
Configuration and state belong to the invoking user. Removing or purging the
package preserves them. Do not delete attempt markers to retry uncertain actions.
.SH SEE ALSO
Installed README.md, NOTICE.md and releases.md in /usr/share/doc/kobra-lan-cli/.
